1
00:00:02,054 --> 00:00:03,228
Hi everyone!

2
00:00:03,294 --> 00:00:06,100
Today, a tutorial on the "cross ride"!

3
00:00:06,166 --> 00:00:14,902
[Music]

4
00:00:14,968 --> 00:00:18,243
As for your hand,
it's easier to put the hand

5
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:21,993
on the side of the leg that goes behind,
the straight one.

6
00:00:22,774 --> 00:00:24,494
So for me, that's my right hand.

7
00:00:25,201 --> 00:00:29,934
To start, you can lean against a wall.
It's a bit like learning to ride.

8
00:00:30,055 --> 00:00:32,523
At first, you hold on to a wall,
then you slowly let go.

9
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:34,834
The saddle moves a bit
like this as you pedal.

10
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:39,307
And when it drifts to the right,
try to push it back toward the middle.

11
00:00:41,501 --> 00:00:45,634
To start, it's easier

12
00:00:46,307 --> 00:00:48,728
to set the cranks...

13
00:00:48,954 --> 00:00:51,595
The cranks are like this for small hops.

14
00:00:51,794 --> 00:00:54,701
I'll turn them the other way round,
so I do a half-turn.

15
00:00:55,607 --> 00:00:58,261
There, like that, with the crank in front.

16
00:00:58,661 --> 00:01:03,554
To get on, put all your weight
on the front crank

17
00:01:03,647 --> 00:01:07,608
with the opposite foot,
get on, put all your weight on it,

18
00:01:07,674 --> 00:01:12,381
then put your other foot behind,
with the leg straight.

19
00:01:12,821 --> 00:01:17,332
Once you're set up like this,
shift your heel

20
00:01:17,398 --> 00:01:20,261
on the front crank
to get all your weight on the pedal.

21
00:01:20,641 --> 00:01:23,821
See that little movement,
with all the weight on the crank,

22
00:01:23,887 --> 00:01:28,341
and bam, I shift my heel
so I'm in the right spot to ride.

23
00:01:28,574 --> 00:01:33,285
At first, the position will feel weird,
because your back leg stays straight

24
00:01:33,391 --> 00:01:35,075
the whole time you pedal.

25
00:01:35,507 --> 00:01:38,410
So you have to work
with just your ankles.

26
00:01:38,434 --> 00:01:41,208
Sometimes that helps,
but for the back leg,

27
00:01:41,581 --> 00:01:47,088
it's a bit like riding with straight legs.

28
00:01:47,114 --> 00:01:48,848
You keep your knees locked...

29
00:01:49,288 --> 00:01:53,427
And the ankle movement
is exactly the same as in "cross ride".

30
00:01:54,081 --> 00:01:56,840
Now you can ride along walls
like that.

31
00:01:56,906 --> 00:02:06,421
[Music]

32
00:02:06,487 --> 00:02:09,655
The easiest way back onto the pedals
is through a "crank idle".

33
00:02:09,947 --> 00:02:14,188
It's exactly the same steps,
but in reverse.

34
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:17,893
Which means, once you're done pedaling,

35
00:02:19,007 --> 00:02:20,663
or rather, when you want to switch back,

36
00:02:20,949 --> 00:02:27,329
you need your front leg, this one here,

37
00:02:27,395 --> 00:02:32,880
out front, with its pedal forward,
then shift your heel back,

38
00:02:34,414 --> 00:02:36,614
bring the saddle to the side of your hip,

39
00:02:36,687 --> 00:02:40,887
put all your weight on the crank,
take your back foot off...

40
00:02:41,894 --> 00:02:43,980
Sorry... Take your back foot off,

41
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:49,660
and shift the toe of your other foot
so you can put it on the pedal.

42
00:02:49,726 --> 00:03:16,315
[Music]

43
00:03:16,381 --> 00:03:19,514
There are several variations
of the "cross ride".

44
00:03:20,014 --> 00:03:24,900
There's the "backward cross ride",

45
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:29,988
[Music]

46
00:03:30,487 --> 00:03:32,820
there's the "drag seat" version,

47
00:03:36,641 --> 00:03:42,340
and also the "cross ride spin". That's it.

48
00:03:42,406 --> 00:03:52,913
[Music]

